{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGLWeyl","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGLWeyl","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.normaliser_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.normaliser_eq","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L198-L217","doc":"**The normaliser is forced to be `[d]_{q²}^n`.**  If at size `n = m + 1` the weights of a Markov\ntrace are `s_λ / Z` for a single `Z ≠ 0`, then `Z = [d]_{q²}^n`: `tr(1) = 1` and the character\nidentity leave no freedom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.markov_tr_blockE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.markov_tr_blockE","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L184-L196","doc":"**The actual Ocneanu weight of `λ`** under any Markov trace at Wenzl's level-`d` parameter:\n`tr(E_{λ,t}) = s_λ(1, q², …, q^{2(d−1)}) / [d]_{q²}^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.sum_card_mul_schurPrincipal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.sum_card_mul_schurPrincipal","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L168-L182","doc":"**The Schur–Weyl character identity at the principal specialisation, derived**:\n`Σ_{λ ⊢ n} f^λ s_λ(1, q², …, q^{2(d−1)}) = [d]_{q²}^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.sum_blockE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.sum_blockE","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L153-L166","doc":"**The block idempotents sum to `1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.sum_single_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.sum_single_diag","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L141-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.qtr_jimbo_blockE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.qtr_jimbo_blockE","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L126-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.heckeProduct_blockE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.heckeProduct_blockE","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L116-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.blockE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.blockE","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L109-L114","doc":"A fixed block idempotent `E_{λ,t}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.qtr_jimbo_blockIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JimboGL.qtr_jimbo_blockIdempotent","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JimboGLWeyl.lean#L50-L89","doc":"**The `K`-graded multiplicity of `S_λ` in `(K^d)^{⊗n}` is `s_λ(1, q², …, q^{2(d−1)})`.**\n\nFor the block idempotent `E` (seminormal image `E_{tt}` in block `λ`, `0` in every other block),\n`E² = E` and `Tr(K^{⊗(m+1)} ρ(E)) = schurPrincipal d (q²) λ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}